/-- solkey `SolcControlFlow.ternarySelectsValueByFlag` (`solc/SolcControlFlow.sol`).

solc: expressions/conditional_expression_storage_memory_1.sol — the branch selection on
its own, over plain values rather than references.

concretized: solkey proves this for all parameters; ported at cond = 0.

solkey tags this `@custom:key box`; the port makes its assumptions true
instead, so the diamond also proves that it does not revert. -/
theorem ternarySelectsValueByFlag :
    Diamond State.solcControlFlowStore
    sol[SolcControlFlow]{
      uint cond = 0;
      bool c = cond == 1;
      uint r = c ? 11 : 22;
      assert(r == 22);
    } := by
  corpus_decide solcControlFlowStore_eq

/-- solkey `SolcControlFlow.chainedIfsSelectLastMatch` (`solc/SolcControlFlow.sol`).

solc: expressions/conditional_expression_storage_memory_1.sol — the upstream result is
read back through a chain of independent `if`s, the last matching one winning. -/
theorem chainedIfsSelectLastMatch :
    Diamond State.solcControlFlowStore
    sol[SolcControlFlow]{
      target.a = 2;
      uint t = target.a;
      uint r = 0;
      if (t == 1) { r = 1; };
      if (t == 2) { r = 2; };
      assert(r == 2);
    } := by
  corpus_decide solcControlFlowStore_eq

/-- solkey `SolcControlFlow.nestedIfElseSelectsBranch` (`solc/SolcControlFlow.sol`).

solc: expressions/conditional_expression_multiple.sol — the same branch structure as a
nested `if`/`else` rather than a nested `?:`.

concretized: solkey proves this for all parameters; ported at x = 500.

solkey tags this `@custom:key box`; the port makes its assumptions true
